      "message": "We can also add some tests for this code. Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nCurrently, `cli_test.cc` only tests the path where the command fails with `Error::kNoSuchDevice` (simulating the expected USB drop during a reboot). Both `SwitchMcuMode_EnterBoot` and `SwitchMcuMode_EnterRom` trigger this path by explicitly calling `fake-\u003eFailSendOnCommand(1)`.\n\nHowever, the tests **do not cover** the two other possible paths for `command_accepted`:\n\n1. **Perfect Success:** The switch command succeeds perfectly (no USB drop detected before the function returns).\n2. **Exhausted Retries:** The command fails with an *unexpected* error (like `kResultFail` from a bad response), loops 5 times, and correctly returns `std::unexpected(Error::kResultFail)`.\n\n\n```\nTEST(CliTest, SwitchMcuMode_SuccessWithoutDisconnect) {\n  auto transport \u003d std::make_unique\u003cFakeEcTransport\u003e();\n  auto* fake \u003d transport.get();\n  UsbDevice device \u003d MakeDevice(std::move(transport));\n\n  // Queue valid responses for both the build version check and the switch command.\n  fake-\u003eAddResponse(BuildStringResponse(\"ft9001_v1.0\"));\n  fake-\u003eAddResponse(BuildEmptySuccessResponse());\n\n  auto result \u003d SwitchMcuMode(device, DeviceMode::kEc, Command::kEnterBoot);\n  \n  EXPECT_TRUE(result.has_value());\n}\n\nTEST(CliTest, SwitchMcuMode_FailsAfterMaxRetries) {\n  auto transport \u003d std::make_unique\u003cFakeEcTransport\u003e();\n  auto* fake \u003d transport.get();\n  UsbDevice device \u003d MakeDevice(std::move(transport));\n\n  // Provide a response only for the initial build version check. \n  // Omitting the response for the switch command forces a timeout, causing \n  // the retry loop to exhaust its attempts and fail gracefully.\n  fake-\u003eAddResponse(BuildStringResponse(\"ft9001_v1.0\"));\n\n  auto result \u003d SwitchMcuMode(device, DeviceMode::kEc, Command::kEnterBoot);\n  \n  EXPECT_FALSE(result.has_value());\n  EXPECT_EQ(result.error(), Error::kResultFail);\n}\n```",
