      "message": "The `DeviceMode` enum contains two states that are completely unused anywhere in the logic: `kUnknown` and `kForceUpdate`.\n\nWhen `GetDeviceMode` encounters an unrecognized device, it correctly returns `std::unexpected(Error::kNoSuchDevice)` rather than `kUnknown`, rendering `kUnknown` entirely dead code. Keeping the state machine strictly to the 4 actionable states prevents future switch-statement warnings.\n\n**In `util/focaltech/usb_device.h`:**\n\n```\n--- a/util/focaltech/usb_device.h\n+++ b/util/focaltech/usb_device.h\n@@ -17,12 +17,10 @@\n namespace focaltech {\n \n enum class DeviceMode {\n-  kUnknown,\n   kRom,\n   kBoot,\n   kTest,\n   kEc,\n-  kForceUpdate,\n };\n\n```",
